# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read this before editing the patterns above.
#
# `R CMD build` does NOT parse this file. It calls `readLines` on it and passes
# every non-empty line to `grepl` as a PCRE, so a `#` line is a *pattern*, not a
# comment. That is why the prose below is written without parentheses, brackets,
# asterisks or backslashes: balanced prose is a valid regex that matches no file
# path, whereas one unclosed bracket is a PCRE compile error that fails the build
# outright. `tools:::inRbuildignore` is the function to read if you want to see it.
#
# So: no parentheses in these comments, not even when quoting code. Refer to a
# function by bare name. Where a longer explanation would need punctuation this
# file cannot carry, put it in the commit message or in docs/ instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything under data/ is left out of the source tarball. Two different reasons,
# and they matter differently.
#
# First: humanSkin.rda, wound.rda and visium.rds are 70 MB of real single-cell
# benchmark input. Nothing in R, tests or vignettes reads them, and
# scripts/fetch_ci_fixtures.sh fetches each by a pinned file id with a size and
# sha256 assertion, so they are fetched rather than committed.
#
# Second: the CellChatDB and PPI .rda files are byte-identical duplicates of the
# copies in inst/upstream, which still ship. Keeping both is what puts this
# tarball over CRAN's 5 MB limit -- 8.0 MB with them, 4.9 MB without. Of the two
# copies the datasets are the cheaper to lose, because inst/upstream is what all
# four tests/test files diff against; drop that instead and R CMD check runs no
# tests at all. tests/test-public-surface.R still asserts the datasets are
# byte-identical to upstream, loading them from inst/upstream rather than via the
# data route, so only the data route is given up.

# tests/parity is 470 KB of oracle generators and differential gates. It needs the
# pinned upstream tree at run time, and R CMD check never runs it: the package's
# own test targets are the four tests/test scripts. CI drives tests/parity with
# CELLCHAT_SRC set. The files stay in the repository, which is where the audit
# trail lives.

# Any R CMD build output left in the source directory. This has to be here and not
# only in .gitignore, because R CMD build does not read .gitignore: a stale
# tarball is packaged into the next build. A cellchatrs_0.1.0.tar.gz was 5.7 MB of
# a 13.8 MB tarball, and it recursed -- it contained a copy of the package.
# The pattern is name-agnostic on purpose, since the package has been renamed
# more than once and a pattern naming either name silently stops matching.

# tests/fixtures in its entirety, not just its largest members. These are cargo
# test inputs read by relative path from a checkout; nothing in the installed
# package or in the four R test targets reads them. They stay in the repository
# because they are what makes the bit-identity claim auditable, and
# scripts/gen_fixtures.sh regenerates them from the pinned upstream.